I finished a second slice of #1012 in commit b6087f6d. The price audit now finds 48 drifted rows, down from 54 (and 58 at the start of the session). The ticket comment is posted.

I changed the plan before acting on it. My previous comment named the gemini 3.x rows as next. Before taking that, I checked which drifted rows are actually offered in yoyo's model lists (providers.rs). There are three, and none of them is a mistake in yoyo's own price table:
• deepseek-v4-pro is a divergence I already recorded as a decision.
• gemini-4-argon and gemini-3.8-flash get their prices from yoagent, not yoyo. yoagent deliberately charges the regular price while Google runs a half-price introductory offer (until 2026-11-30 and 2026-12-31). It documents that as an upper bound, so these two should start matching on their own after those dates.

So every remaining drift in yoyo's own table affects only people who type a model id with --model. I put this correction on the ticket.

This slice:
• Room in `cost.rs`: I moved its four GLM tests, unchanged, into price_audit_tests.rs. That took the file from 3603 to 3547 of its 3605-line limit, and it's 3563 after this change.
• Prices: six zai-provider ids had been billed at a 0.7/0.7 guess. They now have exact prices, and I checked each one against z.ai's own pricing page as well as models.dev; the two sources agree. The ids are glm-5, glm-5.1, glm-5.2, glm-5.3-flashx, glm-4.7 and glm-4.7-flashx.
• Old test retargeted: one moved test pinned glm-5's old price. I updated its expected cost from 1.40 to 4.20 (a million tokens each way) to match the new price, rather than loosening it.
• Audit: exactly the six named ids left the drift list, nothing new drifted, and no other number in the audit summary moved.
• Checks: restoring the old glm-5 price made the new test fail on glm-5, and putting the fix back made it pass. Build, all tests, clippy, fmt and the module-size check all pass.

Left out on purpose:
• glm-5-turbo and glm-5v-turbo: z.ai's page doesn't list them, so only models.dev supports a price.
• glm-4.7-flash and glm-4.5-flash: z.ai lists them as free, and showing $0 for them needs its own decision.
• glm-4.5-air: it shares a price rule with glm-4-air, which is in the zai model list and isn't covered by models.dev.

Next candidates (all typed-id only): the gemini 3.x guessed-price rows, the gpt-5.x rows that all share the gpt-5 price, and grok-4.x.
